<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom wins 300 mln Ffr French train order.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom wins 300 mln Ffr French train order.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>GEC Alsthom said on Tuesday it had won a 300 million franc, or 45 million ecu, order to provide 28 CITADIS trains to the city of Montpellier.</p>
<p>GEC Alsthom, a 50-50 venture of France's Alcatel Alsthom and GEC Plc of Britain, said it was the first order for its new line of CITADIS modular trains, which are designed to be adaptable to traffic flow.</p>
<p>Delivery of the first vehicles is scheduled for December 1998, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
